{
  "title": "Pangea™ Distal Medial Tibia Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423209/pangea-tm--distal-medial-tibia-plate",
  "subtitle": "Tibial Shaft Fractures Updated: Jun 8 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 distal tibia plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Distal Anterolateral Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Medial Tibia (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Posterior Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423209/images/0f860df8-2906-4004-9126-a5afcfc9d755_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.31.30_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular holes that accommodate screws are universal; accepting non-locking screws and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**1.6mm K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423209/images/b1ffb69b-488a-465f-ac51-3d88ea36b5c5_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.31.37_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**K-Wire Holes at Distal Aspect**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Single Distal Variable Angle Locking Screw Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed for unicortical capture of the medial malleolus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423209/images/b1ffb69b-488a-465f-ac51-3d88ea36b5c5_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.31.37_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This plate is placed on the medial surface of the distal tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Position is achieved when the distal end of the plate is over the medial malleolus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal Medial Tibia plate designed for fixation of varus failure injuries of the distal tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plate contour is SOMA designed to reduce potential for malrotation of the medial malleolus fragment. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SOMA analysis shows Distal Medial Tibia plate fits closer to bone compared to Synthes VA-LCP distal medial tibia plates. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard medial or anteromedial approach to the distal medial tibia. Care must be taken to protect the saphenous vein and saphenous nerve.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard plate lengths: 3-18 hole (97-307mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Thickness: Shaft 3.3mm, Distal 1.6mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T15: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T8: Ø2.0mm x 135mm (542000(S)) Ø2.0mm x 175mm (542001(S))",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
